---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, withBase } from '../lib/github';

const mail = `mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Semper handles authentication, storage, data policy, and privacy."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 3rem">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p class="sub">Sign-in, where data lives, what we collect, and how you erase it.</p>

    <ul class="privacy-toc">
      <li><a href="#authentication">Authentication</a></li>
      <li><a href="#data-storage">Data storage</a></li>
      <li><a href="#data-policy">Data policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="#privacy-policy">Privacy policy</a></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="prose">
      <h3 id="authentication">Authentication</h3>
      <p>Sign in with Google or email and password.</p>
      <p>
        Email passwords need 8+ characters with upper and lower case, a digit, and a special
        character. <strong>Generate secure password</strong> can fill one in.
      </p>
      <p>
        After email sign-up, open the verification link, then sign in. Unverified accounts cannot
        sign in.
      </p>
      <p>
        New accounts show <strong>Pending approval</strong>. An admin must approve you. Tap
        <strong>Check status</strong> after approval — the screen does not poll.
      </p>
      <p>
        Offline use works if this device was approved before. Import and solve need no network.
        Uploads wait until you are online.
      </p>
      <p>
        To delete your account, open Settings → Your data. Semper re-checks identity on the sign-in
        screen first.
      </p>
      <p>
        After you confirm, it erases cloud backup, this device&apos;s data, and the sign-in, then
        signs you out. If the cloud is unreachable, nothing is deleted.
      </p>
      <p>
        Step-by-step: <a href={withBase('/manual/getting-started')}>Manual · Getting started</a>.
      </p>

      <h3 id="data-storage">Data storage</h3>
      <p>DIC correlation runs only on the phone. The cloud never recomputes fields.</p>
      <p>Analyses stay on the device by default.</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Save to cloud</strong> (optional) queues backups when online.
        <strong>Wi-Fi only</strong> holds uploads until Wi-Fi.
      </p>
      <p>
        A backup is the analysis package you already computed (frames and results). Account and
        device metadata live with the backend.
      </p>
      <p>
        Image bytes are not processed by the API. The client uploads them to org storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        Settings → Analyses data management lists local and cloud rows. You can back up, restore, or
        delete per row.
      </p>

      <h3 id="data-policy">Data policy</h3>
      <p><strong>What we collect</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Account identity from Firebase Auth (email; name when the provider supplies it).</li>
        <li>
          A random device id (not IMEI, serial, or MAC), plus model and OS version for device
          binding.
        </li>
        <li>
          Analysis backups when cloud backup is on (frames and results you choose to sync).
        </li>
        <li>
          Support mail you send — the app can attach account, device id, app version, and phone
          model.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Why</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Sign-in, email verification, and admin approval.</li>
        <li>Optional backup and restore.</li>
        <li>Private account support.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Your controls</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Leave cloud backup off. No new uploads are queued.</li>
        <li>Delete local only, cloud backup only, or everywhere — read the dialog.</li>
        <li>Delete the account to erase cloud copy, device data, and sign-in.</li>
        <li>Email <a href={mail}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> for private account issues.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Community posts (Q&amp;A, bugs, features) go to GitHub. That content follows GitHub&apos;s
        terms, not this backup path.
      </p>

      <h3 id="privacy-policy">Privacy policy</h3>
      <p>
        Semper is provided by IndicVision. Contact: <a href={mail}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>We do not sell your account or analysis data.</p>
      <p>
        We keep account and backup data while your account exists, or until you delete a backup or
        the account.
      </p>
      <p>
        After account erasure, sign-in and stored backups for that account are removed as described
        under Authentication.
      </p>
      <p>
        Correlation runs on device. Optional cloud backup stores what you sync so you can restore
        it — not so the cloud can re-run DIC.
      </p>
      <p>Material changes to this page will be posted here.</p>
      <p>Last updated: 3 Aug 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
